{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]How long, LORD, [Eb]must I call for help
[Gm]I cry out to [Eb]you, Violence!
[Bb]Why do you make me [Eb]see wrongdoing?
De[Gm]struction and vio[Eb]lence are before [F]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The [Eb]law goes numb, [F]justice never comes forth
[Gm]The wicked hem in the [Fsus4]righteous
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]But the righteous shall [Bb]live by his [Eb]faith
The vision a[Gm]waits its appointed [F]time
Look at [Bb]the proud one, his soul is [Eb]not upright
[Gm]The righteous [F]shall live by his [Bb]faith [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Look among the nations and watch
[Eb]Be astonished, be astounded
[Gm]I am doing a work in your days
[Eb]You would not be[F]lieve if it were [Eb]told
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]But the righteous shall [Bb]live by his [Eb]faith
The vision a[Gm]waits its appointed [F]time
Look at the [Bb]proud one, his soul is not [Eb]upright
The [Gm]righteous shall live [F]by his [Bb]faith
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Though the fig tree does not blos[Gm]som
And the [F]vines bear no [Eb]fruit
Yet I will exult in the LORD
[Gm]I will re[F]joice in the [Eb]God of my salva[F]tion
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The LORD God is my [Bb]strength
[Eb]He makes my feet like the [Gm]feet of a deer
[Eb]Sets me up[F]on the [Bb]heights
{end_of_verse}

